ce investigation before capital deployment. DCAD data is completely absent—no property address, no account number, no legal description provided despite a $10,723.97 filing amount. This filing amount suggests either a vacant residential lot in a tertiary Dallas County location or a highly distressed structure with minimal improvement value. The tax breakdown totals only $2,507.59 in base taxes across entities (Dallas County $551.87, Parkland $579.23, Dallas College $287.45, School Equalization $12.59), meaning $8,216.38 of the filing represents accumulated penalties, interest, attorney fees, and court costs—a penalty-to-tax ratio of 3.27:1 indicating multi-year delinquency likely spanning 4-5 years. James Roger Lacy, Jr appears as primary defendant with four additional defendants (BREON CHARLES ODIE, DRIEYONA JANAY LOWE, JENNIFER KAY WESLEY, THERESA BELL LACY), suggesting either an informal family succession situation following a death without probate, a property passed through generations without clear title work, or possibly a tenant/occupant situation where multiple parties have claimed interest. The presence of "THERESA BELL LACY" with matching surname suggests widow or former spouse, while younger-generation names indicate potential heirs or family members who inherited without formal estate administration. Without DCAD physical data, we cannot determine land vs structure play, but the modest tax amount ($551.87 county tax) suggests either county appraisal value near $25,000-$35,000 or a homestead exemption scenario masking higher value.\n\n## FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nFiled amount stands at $10,723.97 as of May 2026, with live tax balance likely reaching $12,500-$13,200 today (December 2026) after seven months of 12% annual post-judgment interest accrual and additional 2026 tax year delinquency. The penalty composition reveals aggressive collection posture: base taxes of $2,507.59 ballooned to $10,723.97 through $8,216.38 in penalties/interest/fees, representing 327% markup. Breaking down entity exposure: Dallas County claims $966.66 (with $414.79 penalties on $551.87 base), Parkland Hospital $1,015.87 ($436.64 penalties on $579.23 base), Dallas College $503','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-07T22:46:52.207809','2026-07-07T22:46:52.207809','2026-07-07T22:46:52.207809',1,'individual','high','','',NULL,NULL);
INSERT INTO cases VALUES(43,'TX-26-00879','116th District Court','GINSBERG, CARL','2026-05-01','OPEN','TAX DELINQUENCY','Armandina De La Rocha, as Co-Trustee of the Armandina and Jose De La Rocha Revocable Trust','[{"name": "Armandina De La Rocha, as Co-Trustee of the Armandina and Jose De La Rocha Revocable Trust", "address": "101 S. Montclair Ave., Dallas, TX 75208", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "Private Process Server", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Unexecuted citation returned 06/01/2026"}, {"name": "Jose De La Rocha, as Co-Trustee of the Armandina and Jose De La Rocha Revocable Trust", "address": "101 S. Montclair Ave., Dallas, TX 75208", "serviceStatus": "unserved", "serviceMethod": "Private Process Server", "isInRemOnly": false, "notes": "Unexecuted citation returned 06/01/2026"}, {"name": "The United States of America", "address": "1100 Commerce Street, Third Floor, Dallas, TX 75242", "serviceStatus": "served", "serviceMethod": "Private Process Server", "isInRemOnly": true, "notes": "Executed citation 06/09/2026; served via Nancy E. Larson, U.S. Attorney for Northern District of Texas"}]','',NULL,'','LGBS (Linebarger)','ATKINS, ASHLY STEELE',19569.63000000000008,NULL,'[]',3,0,0,'[]',0,0,0,'Two primary defendants (Armandina and Jose De La Rocha) remain unserved after initial citation attempts. Only the USA (In Rem Only) was successfully served.','high',NULL,NULL,'none',NULL,0,'2027-01-19',NULL,NULL,NULL,'dallas',NULL,'[{"entity": "Dallas County", "taxAmt": 1258.65, "penaltyInterest": 596.14, "total": 1854.79}, {"entity": "Parkland Hospital District", "taxAmt": 1259.63, "penaltyInterest": 602.21, "total": 1861.84}, {"entity": "Dallas College", "taxAmt": 629.87, "penaltyInterest": 300.57, "total": 930.44}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**PC PEAK DEVELOPMENT – TAX FORECLOSURE ACQUISITION UNIT**\n\n**CASE:** TX-26-00879 | 116th District Court | Judge Ginsberg  \n**SUBJECT PROPERTY:** 101 S. Montclair Ave., Dallas, TX 75208  \n**DATE:** Analysis Current as of Case Filing + 7 Months\n\n---\n\n## 1. PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThe $19,569.63 filing amount against 101 S. Montclair Avenue represents a sophisticated ownership structure now in distress: a revocable trust with co-trustees Armandina and Jose De La Rocha. The Dallas County tax breakdown shows $3,148.15 in base taxes across three entities (County $1,258.65, Parkland $1,259.63, Dallas College $629.87) with penalties adding $1,498.92, suggesting approximately 2-3 years of accumulated delinquency before attorney fees and court costs ballooned the total. Without DCAD account data visible, the $19,569.63 filing strongly implies this is an improved structure play rather than raw land—land-only parcels in this Oak Cliff neighborhood rarely generate tax bills exceeding $3,100 annually. The Montclair Avenue corridor features post-war single-family homes built 1940-1960, typically 1,200-1,500 SF on 5,000-6,500 SF lots. If we reverse-engineer from the County''s $1,258.65 portion (Dallas County rate approximately 0.231%), the assessed value sits around **$545,000**, suggesting either significant appreciation in the hot Oak Cliff market or recent improvements. The revocable trust structure indicates estate planning by elderly owners, and the dual co-trustee setup with both names active (not a survivor situation) suggests either both are alive but financially overwhelmed, or the trust administration has broken down. Federal involvement (USA served as in rem defendant on 06/09/2026) signals a **probable IRS lien** on the property, which dramatically changes the acquisition calculus—any federal tax lien survives foreclosure and attaches to subsequent purchasers unless the redemption period is respected. The unserved status of both primary defendants despite returned citations (06/01/2026) could indicate the De La Rochas are no longer at the property—deceased, relocated to assisted living, or otherwise unreachable at 101 S. Montclair.\n\n## 2. FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nCurrent live tax balance as of December 2026 (7 months post-filing) is approximately **$23,400-','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-07T22:47:42.890968','2026-07-07T22:47:42.890968','2026-07-07T22:47:42.890968',1,'individual','high','','',NULL,NULL);
