ys. Payment history tells the distress story: LV Assets Company LLC paid 2022 taxes (likely a servicer managing distressed notes), then we see Midland Mortgage entries from 1999—suggesting a mortgage default cycle that''s been brewing for 25+ years. Prior related suit **TX-16-02135** from 2016 means these owners have dodged tax foreclosure once already (10 years ago), paid enough to dismiss, then immediately re-defaulted. The apartment address (Apt. 17892, Partridge Loop, Laredo) suggests the Trevinos relocated 150+ miles south and abandoned this Dallas property to tenant chaos or vacancy. With $193.3k value on 850 sqft, we''re looking at $227/sqft—this is pure land value in a gentrifying Dallas pocket where builders would scrape and build 1,600-2,000 sqft new construction.\n\n## FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nFiled amount was **$22,490** (June 2026), but live DCAD balance currently sits at **$18,226.42**—a $4,263.58 reduction suggesting either a partial payment post-filing or DCAD penalty recalculation, though Linebarger''s case total won''t automatically adjust. Breaking down the filing: Dallas ISD carries $10,143.23 ($6,531.70 base + $3,611.53 penalties/interest at 55% penalty ratio), City of Dallas holds $7,018.65 ($4,534.04 base + $2,484.61 penalties at 55% penalty ratio). These penalty ratios indicate **4-5 years of delinquency** despite only filing suit in 2','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-07T22:57:29.636802','2026-07-07T23:24:46.031347','2026-07-07T23:24:46.031347',1,'individual','high','','{"account_number": "00000442985000000", "market_value": 193300, "land_value": 60000, "improvement_value": 133300, "estimated_annual_taxes": 4304.23, "year_built": 1940, "effective_year_built": 1940, "actual_age": 86, "building_class": "04", "construction_type": "FRAME", "foundation": "PIER AND BEAM", "roof_type": "", "roof_material": "", "exterior_wall": "", "living_area_sqft": 850, "total_area_sqft": 850, "bedrooms": 2, "bathrooms": "", "stories": 