 Managing member Tibor Racz operated from 1814 Lucerne St., Dallas 75214 (a residential address, suggesting home-based operations or registered agent address). No real property, no land, no structure — this is uncollectible business equipment debt from a defunct medical practice. The improvement value near zero and no homestead exemption flags in DCAD make sense now: there''s literally no real estate attached to this tax account.\n\n## 2. FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nFiled amount of **$4,540.94** has escalated to **$7,329.43 live balance** as of current data — a 61% penalty acceleration over approximately 11 months. Tax breakdown shows relatively small entity obligations (Dallas County $432.96, Parkland Hospital $454.96, Dallas College $225.68, School Equalization $10.26) with penalties representing 43-44% of the total. However, **this debt is secured only against dissolved business personal property with zero recovery value**. The payoff today ($7,329.43) buys you nothing — no deed, no real property, no collateral. Debt-to-value ratio is infinite (debt divided by zero). Linebarger''s pursuit of this case suggests they''re attempting service on Racz personally at the Lucerne address to potentially pierce corporate veil or obtain personal judgment, but the business entity shield typically protects members from LLC tax debt absent fraud or personal guarantees.\n\n## 3. TIMELINE & URGENCY\n\nAt 11 months from filing (June 2026 to May 2027), this case sits in the middle timeframe before judgment using your benchmarks. Next hearing date **February 15, 2027** has already passed (we''re in May 2027 per context), meaning case likely has post-hearing status we''re not seeing in this snapshot. Critical issue: **','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-07T22:58:03.304043','2026-07-07T22:58:03.304043','2026-07-07T22:58:03.304043',1,'individual','high','','{"account_number": "99201109440000000", "market_value": null, "land_value": null, "improvement_value": null