8.76, "total": 5892.31}]',replace('# ACQUISITION INTELLIGENCE MEMO\n**TX-26-01189 | Jose & Idalia Ortega | 1217 W. Red Bird Ln., Dallas 75232**\n\n## PROPERTY & OWNER SITUATION\n\nThis is a **structure-on-decline play with land residual value focus**. The 1958-built, 2,249 sqft home sits at 50% depreciation after 68 years—functionally at end-of-life for residential lending purposes. No homestead exemption indicates absentee ownership or non-occupancy since the Ortegas acquired the property via deed transfer on 4/14/2009. Payment history tells the story: COUCH PROPERTIES LLP paid 2015 taxes (possibly a failed wholesaler assignment or short-term hold), STEWART TITLE paid 2008 (closing year—Ortegas bought it), and HALL CLAYLIA S paid 2007 (prior owner). The Ortegas went 11 consecutive years without payment post-2015, suggesting complete financial/property abandonment. With market value at $325,200 and typical Red Bird land comprising 35-45% of value, we''re likely looking at $115,000-$146,000 land basis with a tear-down or deep-rehab structure. The improvement-to-land ratio warrants physical inspection, but DCAD''s 50% depreciation flag signals major deferred maintenance—expect foundation issues, obsolete systems, and possible code violations common in 1950s Oak Cliff housing stock.\n\n## FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nFiled amount shows **$18,542.30** with current live balance at **$18,680.34**—a $138 climb in penalty acceleration since filing on 6/16/2026 (we''re currently ~2 weeks post-filing). Breakdown: Dallas County $1,766.89, Parkland $1,765.70, Dallas College $882.11, DISD $5,109+ (truncated in data but likely $11,000-$12,000 based on residual math to reach $18,542 total). Add two State of Texas child support liens from 2013 (file nos. 201300217500 and 201300144433) and state tax liens from 11/16/2020 and 6/8/2022 (file nos. 202000316478 and 202200159541)—amounts unknown but typically $3,000-$15,000 each for Comptroller liens. Conservative total debt exposure: **$18,680 