ife—any buyer will immediately face foundation, electrical, plumbing, and structural obsolescence issues exceeding improvement value. The market value of $120,340 is being propped up by **land value**, not the structure itself. No homestead exemption signals absentee ownership or complete disengagement. \n\nThe ownership chain tells a distress story: **Larry B. Jackson** held this property and paid sporadically (2012, 2013, 2016), then transferred via deed on 5/22/2018 to current owners **Guadalupe Pichardo (50%)** and **Luden Ismael Osorto (50%)**. Zero payments for **8 consecutive years** post-transfer suggests this was either an inheritance situation gone sideways, a failed flip attempt, or a distressed transfer to dodge creditors. Prior suit **TX-11-31461** indicates this property has been in the tax foreclosure system before—this is a repeat offender property with chronic non-payment patterns. The Jacksons remain in rem defendants at a separate Dallas address (6224 Teague Dr.), suggesting clouded title or unrecorded interests. Pichardo''s listed address (6406 Kemrock Dr., Dallas) differs from the subject property, confirming absentee status and disengagement.\n\n---\n\n## 2. FINANCIAL PICTURE\n\nFiled amount was **$15,389.90** on June 16, 2026. Live tax balance as of today sits at **$15,690.92**—a modest $301.02 increase over 7 months, indicating penalties and interest are accruing at roughly 2.4% annually (Texas statutory 12% prorated). The current debt-to-value ratio is **13.04%** ($15,690.92 / $120,340), which represents attractive equity cushion but also signals complete owner capitulation—no one walks away from 87% equity unless the property is unlivable, landlocked, or they','\n',char(10)),NULL,'pre_judgment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-07-07T22:59:59.652004','2026-07-07T23:24:17.230959','2026-07-07T23:24:17.230959',1,'individual','high','','{"account_number": "00000643441000000", "market_value": 120340, "land_value": 70000, "improvement_value": 50340, "est